WEBVTT

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.310
Chihaya...

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:11.240
Gunzou

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:59.680
You can't fathom the circumstance of birth

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:19.800
As a worrywart, you come to this place helplessly

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:33.110
Across the cold blue sky, scattered fragments of sadness are floating in the air

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:39.140
Blue Snow

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:48.750
Where are you coming from, where are you disappearing to

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:54.100
Blue Snow

00:03:54.240 --> 00:04:04.040
I can still gently feel

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:11.830
homey atmosphere in my hand.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:28.700
Blue Snow

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:48.940
Blue Snow

00:04:49.040 --> 00:05:00.380
ARPEGGIO of BLUE STEEL

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:08.780
The era of humanity has ended.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:19.520
During the year 2039,

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:23.300
a critical rise in sea level occurs beyond humanity's expectation.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.800
As we are trying to seek out a solution,

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:34.660
the Fleet of Fog appears and blockades our
aviation-marine freedom and communication.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:38.280
The origin and purpose of our enemy is unknown.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:45.020
We can't even recall why we named them "The Fleet of Fog".

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:48.580
Although their battleships look old-fashioned,

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:54.400
their weapons are far more advanced  than anything we have.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:56.340
No matter what strategy we use,

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.000
they'll wipe us out like an ant.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:03.300
Helplessly, the world starts to lose hope.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:15.800
During my training at Marine Technical Academy
to become a marine cadet officer someday,

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:20.640
I visited a top-secret military warehouse and

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.600
make the first contact with the Fog.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.740
This is a captured Fog ship.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:33.160
Although its appearance closely resembles that of a Pacific War submarine,

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.940
it is not of human origin.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.240
An enemy of humanity...

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:43.820
A human.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:48.340
Chihaya Gunzou...

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:56.360
That's also my first contact with submarine I-401.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:05.500
Here I am. Now let's hear your reason for dragging me out here.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.640
To be precise, I am the one who has been waiting.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:12.400
I have been isolated from the outside world for seven years.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.700
Seven years?

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:15.030
Who are you?

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:19.400
I obey the orders I have been given... I am a tool.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:21.730
What...

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.120
What are you?

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:28.980
Chihaya Gunzou.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.760
I have been ordered to obey you.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:33.860
I know nothing else.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:38.920
Inquiry: what is your purpose?

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:41.060
My purpose?

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:45.960
I...

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:55.320
I want the strength to break the status quo.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:58.200
Understood.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.560
The 401...

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:20.420
This is me.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.240
Are you with the Fog?

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.100
Yes.

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:27.020
The enemy?

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.320
I don't know.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:33.640
I only know one thing: I must make contact with you and obey.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:37.700
That is the only order that remains in my memory.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:43.720
We are weapons. We engage in battle under orders.

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:45.460
That is our entire existence.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:49.060
That is why we desire orders.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:52.360
401.

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.420
Become my ship!

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:07.720
Gunzou.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:11.960
Board me.

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:18.000
A new weapon? A torpedo?

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.460
It seems they have finished analyzing the Fog's corrosive torpedo

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:23.780
and made further improvements.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:25.940
Much of it is a black box,

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:31.160
but it does seem that Man could strike back if this can be mass produced.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.640
Only if it arrives America safely.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.960
Don't be such a downer.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:40.080
The secret agreement with America was made three months ago,

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.260
after which all communications ceased.
We have no idea about their current situation.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.060
Iona, you really can't tell?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:50.500
I am cut off from the fleet.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:54.000
All I know is what I've been able to detect.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.540
That's true...

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:58.180
And that's why you took the job, Captain?

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:03.840
Yeah, we're the only ones who can make this happen.

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:07.250
The handoff for the new weapon sample will be at the Port of Yokosuka.

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:08.040
Understood.

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:10.320
Setting course for Yokosuka.

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:14.360
Let's go retrieve humanity's last hope.

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:32.880
I've become quite used to this embodied existence.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:36.740
Fleet of Fog: Pacific Patrol Fleet 1 Flagship
Battleship Kongo

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.780
What a disgrace.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.700
We are weapons.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:39.620
Takao.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.440
I see.

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:44.580
401 is on the move, isn't she?

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:47.600
Traitor, siding with the humans...

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:52.250
Fleet of Fog: Pacific Patrol Fleet 1
Heavy Cruiser Takao

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:51.760
I shall reduce you to dust.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:57.540
We are currently within  Typhoon 11's storm zone.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:01.750
Plan A involves maintaining our heading along the typhoon's path, then turning north,

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:04.610
avoiding detection by Takao and entering the Port of Yokosuka.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:06.580
That plan's already bust.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:08.070
That leaves us with Plan B.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:11.180
Leave the typhoon, circle around Takao's picket line,

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:12.980
and approach Yokosuka.

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:15.900
If she pursues us, we may arrive in Yokosuka

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:18.460
with Takao still hot on our heels.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.280
That brings us to Plan C.

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:24.920
We defeat Takao here.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:28.880
We're talking a heavy cruiser here!

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:41.180
I see.

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:43.200
So that's the real 401.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.500
Engage!

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:10.320
First, I'll drop your Klein Field to critical levels with one blow.

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:13.240
Gunzou.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.340
No, it's nothing.

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:24.580
I won't be like Hyuga.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:27.300
Depth 15.

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:31.720
Hurry up to the surface, 401.

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:33.420
Depth 10.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:34.720
Approaching surface.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.300
That's it...

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.180
Yes, that's the way...

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:45.060
Countdown surfacing, 3... 2... 1....

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:46.080
Surface.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.660
Sidekick, hard to port!

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:52.040
Sidekick, hard to port!

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:03.420
Reverse floats! Maximum output! Crash dive!

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:05.420
Launch everything we've got!

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:08.000
Takao knows our precise location!

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:17.630
I missed?

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:21.680
My timing for the supergravity cannon should have been perfect...

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:22.760
But.

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:28.300
Can you hide yourself from all these corrosive torpedoes?

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:32.100
Iona, we're going to use the loot from Hyuga.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:33.340
Okay.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.620
Engine output at maximum! Blow the graviton floats!

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:48.830
All hands, brace yourselves!

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:50.690
Surface at rapid speed!

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.980
Farewell, 401.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:21.020
A supergravity cannon?

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:24.760
Why would a mere patrol submarine have one of those?!

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:26.920
501, emergency evasive maneuvers!

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.110
Sever contacts!

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:42.920
Damn bastard was clinging to Takao to look like there was only one ship!

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:45.580
Locked on Takao along firing axis.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.800
Is that her Mental Model?

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:58.690
Decrease firing angle by three degrees!

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.430
Decreasing angle by three degrees.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.060
But we'll miss Takao

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:02.680
That's fine!

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.320
All hands, brace for imminent shock.

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:14.700
Fire supergravity cannon!

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:16.300
Firing.

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.000
It seems you've lost.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:53.080
It's just a weapons lockdown for 24 hours.

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:57.020
That damned 401 was hiding a supergravity cannon.

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:59.600
But why did she have that?

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:02.260
They must've looted it off Hyuga.

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:05.250
Humans are quite creative.

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:06.720
It was Hyuga's?!

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:10.260
The 401 and Hyuga have engaged in the past.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:12.360
And Hyuga lost.

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:16.260
To suffer theft at the hands of humans... How pathetic.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:21.500
And you were forced by 401 to lock your weapons and retreat to the outer seas.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:24.000
Are you really in a position to belittle Hyuga?

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:29.920
I won't let them get away with this.

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:32.960
This isn't like you.

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:34.920
What are you thinking?

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:37.240
I'll be taking my leave!

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:51.000
If I had a human unit aboard,

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:53.660
I would also be capable of such tactics.

00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:03.420
I, too, want that unit...

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:41.680
Drainage complete.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:43.220
Opening bulkheads.

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:45.800
Commencing descent to dockyard.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:04.100
It's an underground dockyard,

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:07.960
built to protect the remnants of the Japanese fleet from the Fog.

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:25.240
Hey, Iona!

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.820
Can you open up your belly for us?

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:45.060
Sou!

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:48.960
You're in command in my absence.

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:50.540
Understood.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:53.380
I will assume command until you return.

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:11.100
This is a memorial for those who died in the war against the Fog.

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:15.180
It's a cemetery for the navy.

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:16.820
"Cemetery"?

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:21.120
A place to honor the dead and comfort their souls.

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:22.360
The dead...

00:19:22.770 --> 00:19:25.580
Those whose vital functions have ceased?

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:30.940
Is there any meaning in honoring the dead?

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:32.420
Meaning?

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:42.920
The meaning might be to allow those left behind to come to terms with reality.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.180
This is just a random place.

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:49.720
It's in the human nature to
give meaning to random places.

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:53.160
Doing so gives us peace.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.420
A meaningless act.

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:57.400
Meaningless, huh?

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:04.980
Perhaps the act of seeking meaning in meaningless acts is what human evolution is all about.

00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:11.960
That reminds me of the "random noise" generated
by the inevitable degradation of the copying process,

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:16.540
which revitalizes the proliferation system in order to maintain diversity.

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:22.180
Thank you for your business!

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:27.760
"The captain knows everything about his ship."

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:32.120
"It's a necessity in order to make his ship do exactly what he wants."

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:37.160
To do exactly... what he wants...

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:39.420
Come to me, Takao.

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:44.680
To make me... do exactly whatever he wants...

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:53.140
You showed up faster than expected,

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:57.440
Fleet of Fog: Flagship Personal Guard and Intelligence Unit
I-400  I-402

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.600
400, 402.

00:20:57.790 --> 00:21:01.100
We would like to learn your reasons for leaving the fleet.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.460
Since you cut yourself off from the Concept Comm System,

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.760
we had no choice but to come to you.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:11.440
I want to have a captain.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:12.620
A captain?

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.920
Are you referring to Chihaya Gunzou?

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:19.500
He is capable of using me more effectively than even I can.

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:21.780
I want to become stronger.

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:24.580
Quite natural for a weapon, don't you think?

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:27.060
And is this part of a plan of some kind?

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:30.690
I'll come up with a plan later.

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:31.870
So there is none.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.600
You left the Fog without any plan whatsoever?

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:35.540
Shut up!

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:52.060
When I made contact with 401,

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:55.080
I caught a brief glimpse of a place that looked very interesting.

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.220
I will wait for him there.

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:05.420
We will need to continue monitoring the situation.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:07.480
Yes, by using her.

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:09.600
By using her.

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.600
Hey, Kongo, do you know?

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:22.620
Russian put jam in their tea?

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:23.660
"Jam"?

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:25.820
Also known as "preserves"!

00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:28.910
Fleet of Fog: Pacific Patrol Fleet 1
Heavy Cruiser Maya

00:22:25.950 --> 00:22:28.940
A non-perishable food made by boiling fruit and sugar!

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:31.220
What happens when that is added to tea?

00:22:31.400 --> 00:22:32.300
Who knows?

00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:35.800
It just feels more trendy than using these cubes.

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:39.360
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:22:40.280 --> 00:22:42.020
What are you going to do with 401?

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:43.340
I'm going to sink her.

00:22:43.390 --> 00:22:45.160
I have already taken steps.

00:22:47.370 --> 00:22:50.860
Oh, so that's why you sent those two ships.

00:22:51.110 --> 00:22:53.220
Hey, would that count as "tactics"?

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:02.730
Fleet of Fog: Pacific Patrol Fleet 1
Fast Battleship Kirishima

00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:01.560
It's been seven years.

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:06.480
Fleet of Fog: Pacific Patrol Fleet 1
Fast Battleship Haruna

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.060
We've arrived.

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:08.680
Crash dive!

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:09.520
Roger.

00:23:19.350 --> 00:23:20.700
A corrosive torpedo?

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:23.320
Calculating corrosion countermeasures.

00:23:24.210 --> 00:23:26.560
Adjusting Klein Field.

00:23:31.040 --> 00:23:32.630
Corrosive torpedoes, impact confirmed!

00:23:32.650 --> 00:23:35.400
Klein Field deployment by enemy ships, confirmed.

00:23:40.610 --> 00:23:46.140
Yokosuka's defense barrier has vents at regular intervals.

00:23:46.850 --> 00:23:51.690
The sea water entering and exiting through those vents
passes between these scattered buildings,

00:23:51.730 --> 00:23:54.660
which causes complex currents in this entire area.

00:23:55.090 --> 00:23:55.860
I see.

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:58.620
If we move using these currents...

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:03.740
We can get behind the enemy without being detected.

00:24:04.590 --> 00:24:05.400
Gunzou.

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.340
Yeah, the real fight starts now.

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:12.340
We are weapons.

00:24:12.700 --> 00:24:16.520
We should just focus on sinking the enemy before us.

00:24:17.110 --> 00:24:17.980
However,

00:24:19.130 --> 00:24:21.920
Thanatonium readings straight ahead.

00:24:27.180 --> 00:24:28.760
Sonar contact ahead.

00:24:29.040 --> 00:24:31.300
It is too large to be a decoy.

00:24:31.560 --> 00:24:32.980
It must be 401.

00:24:34.410 --> 00:24:37.080
I guess you've given up on hide-and-seek.

00:24:45.960 --> 00:24:46.740
Sink.

00:24:48.780 --> 00:24:49.280
Kirishima!

00:24:58.880 --> 00:25:00.140
From behind?!

00:25:00.620 --> 00:25:02.280
But 401 is in front of us!

00:25:03.670 --> 00:25:05.060
What is that?

00:25:05.770 --> 00:25:07.340
It's the battleship Mikasa,

00:25:07.350 --> 00:25:09.120
launched in 1902.

00:25:09.490 --> 00:25:12.100
It sank along with Old Yokosuka City.

00:25:12.110 --> 00:25:16.140
They scattered active nanomaterial particles on the ship's surface,

00:25:16.460 --> 00:25:18.040
which deceived us.

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:23.260
They're toying with us both, Haruna.

00:25:24.550 --> 00:25:26.320
That's good though  401

00:25:26.990 --> 00:25:31.100
I've never had so much fun.

00:25:31.200 --> 00:25:34.860
That's right. I want to sink her with my own two hands.

00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:36.460
No matter what!

00:25:37.300 --> 00:25:40.920
Kirishima's emotion emulator values are changing rapidly.

00:25:40.980 --> 00:25:43.140
We'll show you who's stronger, 401.

00:25:43.620 --> 00:25:47.320
You, with humans aboard, or us.

00:25:47.910 --> 00:25:48.580
All right.

00:25:49.030 --> 00:25:50.440
I'll join you, Kirishima.

00:25:55.700 --> 00:25:58.330
Hey, this can't be good!

00:25:58.780 --> 00:26:00.980
Detecting gravitons on a massive scale!

00:26:00.980 --> 00:26:02.480
What's this sound?

00:26:02.550 --> 00:26:04.560
The sea will split open.

00:26:38.870 --> 00:26:40.660
Hey, what the hell is that?!

00:26:42.200 --> 00:26:44.330
Th-they've docked together!

00:26:53.910 --> 00:26:56.540
It's over, 401!

00:27:07.730 --> 00:27:10.280
Impossible! Where did that come from?!

00:27:11.840 --> 00:27:15.000
Another launcher... hidden in Mikasa's shadows?

00:27:18.740 --> 00:27:20.610
401!

00:27:25.020 --> 00:27:27.840
Unable to halt... launch sequence.

00:27:28.910 --> 00:27:32.910
We're... going down...

00:27:41.500 --> 00:27:42.260
Haruna...

00:27:43.940 --> 00:27:44.600
No!

00:27:45.580 --> 00:27:48.540
I.... I don't want...

00:27:51.620 --> 00:27:52.920
... to die yet!...

00:27:53.780 --> 00:27:54.580
Ah, so this is...

00:27:55.150 --> 00:27:55.900
This is...

00:27:59.270 --> 00:28:00.060
This is...

00:28:02.080 --> 00:28:04.120
This is... regret.

00:28:26.050 --> 00:28:30.730
Design Child
Osakabe Makie

00:28:27.120 --> 00:28:29.760
Silver sand... nanomaterials.

00:29:08.420 --> 00:29:14.720
Defeated Haruna and Kirishima coincidentally meet the design child.

00:29:16.360 --> 00:29:17.890
Shazam!

00:29:20.610 --> 00:29:22.320
Fast Battleship Kirishima (Yotarou)

00:29:22.390 --> 00:29:23.580
Here, Yotarou.

00:29:28.510 --> 00:29:30.340
We have no choice now!

00:29:30.450 --> 00:29:31.540
Forgive us, Makie!

00:29:31.540 --> 00:29:32.420
Amazing!

00:29:33.880 --> 00:29:39.300
As a robotic child, she's unable to live normally and freely.

00:29:40.180 --> 00:29:43.580
She possesses feelings, unlike a mental model.

00:29:44.710 --> 00:29:45.840
Is this happiness?

00:29:46.510 --> 00:29:48.630
Of course, it's not.

00:30:42.290 --> 00:30:44.750
Every friendship has an end.

00:30:46.500 --> 00:30:50.200
Soon, we start to realize

00:30:51.530 --> 00:30:58.070
leaving a friend behind leaves us nothing

00:30:58.080 --> 00:31:00.880
but pain and sorrow in our existence.

00:31:01.710 --> 00:31:04.330
A warm feeling is slowly budding

00:31:04.340 --> 00:31:09.740
within our heart to protect our precious ones.

00:31:15.740 --> 00:31:16.600
Friends.

00:31:17.600 --> 00:31:21.500
They are those who help and support each other.

00:31:30.540 --> 00:31:31.050
Makie,

00:31:32.430 --> 00:31:33.430
I have a favor to ask.

00:31:34.460 --> 00:31:36.080
Will you be my—

00:31:38.600 --> 00:31:41.300
our friend?

00:31:42.020 --> 00:31:42.610
I'm included?

00:31:43.530 --> 00:31:44.260
Haruharu...

00:31:47.960 --> 00:31:48.480
Okay!

00:31:53.750 --> 00:31:56.140
I ponder my own existence.

00:31:57.050 --> 00:32:00.300
For example, I can feel my existence.

00:32:01.300 --> 00:32:03.580
But, do 'I' really exist?

00:32:05.040 --> 00:32:07.190
Although I'm able to process thoughts,

00:32:07.920 --> 00:32:11.230
it's just because I was programmed to do so.

00:32:10.530 --> 00:32:15.490
Origin Fleet of Fog: Pacific Patrol Fleet 2
Battleship Hyuga

00:32:12.290 --> 00:32:16.690
How can I ever find the truth behind my own existence?

00:32:17.810 --> 00:32:22.810
Who can ever prove that my thoughts
are really mine but not just programs?

00:32:24.100 --> 00:32:27.400
If I'm dreaming, that means I'm sleeping.

00:32:28.320 --> 00:32:32.720
If I'm sleeping now, this whole reality is known as dream.

00:32:33.470 --> 00:32:34.770
Thought becomes reality.

00:32:35.200 --> 00:32:36.500
Reality becomes thought.

00:32:37.360 --> 00:32:40.560
Our deep consciousness circulates continuously.

00:32:40.760 --> 00:32:43.240
We slowly engrave this in our heart.

00:32:44.350 --> 00:32:45.680
There's a phrase,

00:32:46.900 --> 00:32:49.880
"I'm thinking, therefore I do exist".

00:32:50.180 --> 00:32:51.250
Who am I?

00:32:54.050 --> 00:32:56.540
Why did I meet Gunzou?

00:33:01.520 --> 00:33:03.120
H-Haruna...

00:33:04.080 --> 00:33:05.060
I know.

00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:08.260
Kongo!

00:33:09.300 --> 00:33:14.000
Haruna, Kirishima, why are you leaving the fleet?

00:33:15.990 --> 00:33:20.100
Kongo, I will stay with Makie for the time being.

00:33:22.610 --> 00:33:24.220
She severed the comm link.

00:33:25.050 --> 00:33:27.110
And what will you do, Kirishima?

00:33:27.180 --> 00:33:30.760
I-I intend to observe Haruna.

00:33:35.820 --> 00:33:36.480
Maya.

00:33:36.630 --> 00:33:38.000
Yeah, Kongo?

00:33:38.500 --> 00:33:40.460
The situation is as you heard.

00:33:42.240 --> 00:33:44.260
You will rendezvous with me.

00:33:44.490 --> 00:33:47.040
Yay! I finally get some action!

00:33:47.530 --> 00:33:48.960
We are weapons!

00:33:49.150 --> 00:33:52.640
Our directive is to receive and carry out missions!

00:33:54.680 --> 00:33:56.080
It's a carnival!

00:33:59.830 --> 00:34:03.530
Well, Kongo already found us out when Haruna and Kirishima arrived.

00:34:03.550 --> 00:34:06.650
It's just like her to avoid complications.

00:34:12.810 --> 00:34:14.660
Hyuga's signature is still present.

00:34:15.440 --> 00:34:15.960
Maya.

00:34:16.400 --> 00:34:17.270
Right on!

00:34:17.680 --> 00:34:18.810
Leave it to me!

00:34:19.150 --> 00:34:20.970
Zip, zoom!

00:34:23.950 --> 00:34:26.950
Supergravity cannon, fire!

00:34:54.910 --> 00:34:57.660
Right now, I am his ship.

00:34:59.150 --> 00:35:00.730
We are the Blue Steel!

00:35:00.910 --> 00:35:02.840
I can't lose to a ship of the same class.

00:35:03.830 --> 00:35:05.330
I hate you, Takao!

00:35:05.550 --> 00:35:07.140
Sink!

00:35:07.570 --> 00:35:09.460
Love will never sink!

00:35:16.460 --> 00:35:18.500
Every single one of them is breaking...

00:35:19.780 --> 00:35:20.300
Maya.

00:35:20.610 --> 00:35:22.350
Yup, did you call?

00:35:23.030 --> 00:35:25.780
Both Takao and Hyuga are clearly distractions.

00:35:26.370 --> 00:35:27.400
Just leave them be.

00:35:28.310 --> 00:35:32.650
More importantly, deal with the  root cause: 401 and Chihaya Gunzou.

00:35:33.250 --> 00:35:35.070
Kongo, you sound tired.

00:35:35.420 --> 00:35:37.920
Must be tough when
no one will listen to you!

00:35:37.980 --> 00:35:40.230
And what about you, Maya?

00:35:40.570 --> 00:35:41.150
Me?

00:35:41.560 --> 00:35:46.140
I just obey the Admiralty Code and Kongo!

00:35:47.230 --> 00:35:49.660
Indeed.

00:35:50.600 --> 00:35:52.640
That is how the Fog should be.

00:35:53.280 --> 00:35:56.260
We will use the route and coordinates Hyuga provided.

00:35:56.300 --> 00:35:58.740
After using the currents to escape from the danger zone,

00:35:58.750 --> 00:36:01.700
we will head to the rendezvous point to join Takao and the others.

00:36:02.280 --> 00:36:05.320
Takao bought us time so that we could escape.

00:36:05.970 --> 00:36:09.720
We just have to hope that Kongo's fleet will let us go.

00:36:09.950 --> 00:36:11.460
That's too much to ask.

00:36:12.860 --> 00:36:14.420
We have her now.

00:36:33.370 --> 00:36:35.760
Swift and decisive should be the ideal of the warrior.

00:36:35.790 --> 00:36:38.600
I think a human wrote those words in a book.

00:36:38.600 --> 00:36:41.780
Indeed, we of the Fog are weapons.

00:36:41.890 --> 00:36:44.240
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:36:45.430 --> 00:36:47.560
The mines aren't slowing her down.

00:36:52.010 --> 00:36:52.860
Kongo...

00:36:53.590 --> 00:36:55.900
Aren't you hurting yourself?

00:36:56.170 --> 00:36:59.360
To us, pain is an unnecessary concept.

00:37:01.930 --> 00:37:03.800
Thanatonium readings. Twelve contacts.

00:37:03.810 --> 00:37:05.060
Launch passive decoys!

00:37:15.480 --> 00:37:17.100
Remember this.

00:37:18.420 --> 00:37:20.700
I hate you

00:37:37.450 --> 00:37:39.160
Sh-She submerged?

00:37:39.770 --> 00:37:41.900
She's going to give chase underwater!

00:37:41.980 --> 00:37:44.520
Full burst mode critical in T-minus 52 seconds.

00:37:47.400 --> 00:37:50.040
Graviton readings aboard Kongo!

00:37:50.650 --> 00:37:53.660
Does she intend to fire the supergravity cannon at point-blank range?!

00:37:53.670 --> 00:37:54.420
Probably.

00:37:54.780 --> 00:37:56.700
So she'll ram right into us.

00:37:57.200 --> 00:38:00.160
Reallocate Klein Field operations to reaching full burst mode!

00:38:00.250 --> 00:38:01.020
Understood.

00:38:01.220 --> 00:38:04.860
Reallocating all operations not being used for thrust.

00:38:06.940 --> 00:38:09.480
T-minus 30 seconds to critical.

00:38:09.530 --> 00:38:10.080
29...

00:38:15.980 --> 00:38:16.780
Fire.

00:38:20.240 --> 00:38:21.600
What's going on?

00:38:26.690 --> 00:38:27.620
5...

00:38:27.980 --> 00:38:28.850
4...

00:38:29.400 --> 00:38:30.000
3...

00:38:30.740 --> 00:38:31.540
2...

00:38:32.080 --> 00:38:32.900
1...

00:38:33.430 --> 00:38:35.400
Full burst mode critical.

00:38:35.490 --> 00:38:37.780
Get us out of here at full speed!

00:38:48.220 --> 00:38:49.000
Hyuga...

00:38:49.960 --> 00:38:53.020
You dare to hack <i>me</i> behind my back?

00:38:54.840 --> 00:39:00.020
Your normal self wouldn't have fallen for such a simple tactic.

00:39:00.530 --> 00:39:04.600
But maybe you're more human than you'd like to think, huh?

00:39:05.470 --> 00:39:08.160
You didn't sink me, either.

00:39:08.320 --> 00:39:11.300
This must be one of those abnormalities you talked about.

00:39:11.380 --> 00:39:13.550
You made a clear error in judgment.

00:39:13.570 --> 00:39:18.990
Oh, and I guess I can tell you
that the trump card of humanity you were after

00:39:19.280 --> 00:39:21.500
is actually aboard me.

00:39:34.300 --> 00:39:37.590
You are all wrong.

00:39:38.540 --> 00:39:40.040
Wrong.

00:39:43.810 --> 00:39:45.520
Iona?! Are you alright?

00:39:45.960 --> 00:39:50.100
I'm okay. I'm just tired because of the system load.

00:39:50.380 --> 00:39:51.160
I see.

00:39:52.360 --> 00:39:55.400
I am your ship, Gunzou.

00:40:08.700 --> 00:40:09.320
What?!

00:40:16.180 --> 00:40:18.200
An ambush?

00:40:24.720 --> 00:40:26.960
401 confirmed sunk.

00:40:28.120 --> 00:40:29.460
Mission complete.

00:40:33.620 --> 00:40:39.780
We of the Fleet of Fog
obey the Admiralty Code.

00:40:48.710 --> 00:40:53.960
Completed scan of current area
to depth of one thousand meters.

00:40:54.330 --> 00:40:57.200
No sign of 401.

00:40:58.380 --> 00:41:03.920
It seems reasonable to assume that she has been
attacked by someone other than Kongo and Maya.

00:41:04.240 --> 00:41:05.760
This is a real problem.

00:41:06.170 --> 00:41:09.720
The ocean trench in this area can reach
depths of nine thousand meters.

00:41:09.950 --> 00:41:13.200
If she sunk that far,
there's no hope of finding her.

00:41:13.210 --> 00:41:15.160
But we have to try!

00:41:20.210 --> 00:41:22.130
Hey, what do you think you're doing?!

00:41:22.810 --> 00:41:23.810
What else?

00:41:24.210 --> 00:41:26.010
I'm going under to look for her myself!

00:41:26.340 --> 00:41:28.640
Don't be so reckless!

00:41:28.940 --> 00:41:33.040
The ones who attacked Iona may be in hiding somewhere!

00:41:45.020 --> 00:41:47.300
Given the lack of signs of enemy ships on the surface,

00:41:47.360 --> 00:41:49.410
the enemy is probably a submarine.

00:41:49.490 --> 00:41:53.240
A heavy cruiser like you would be at a disadvantage underwater.

00:41:53.750 --> 00:41:54.500
Why...

00:41:55.600 --> 00:41:58.400
Why are you acting like everything's okay?!

00:41:58.710 --> 00:42:02.170
What happened to your crazed infatuation with Iona and all that?

00:42:03.120 --> 00:42:04.630
Of course I'm not okay.

00:42:05.650 --> 00:42:08.910
But my dear Iona entrusted me with the fleet.

00:42:09.470 --> 00:42:13.340
If worst comes to worst, I have to carry on her wishes.

00:42:16.430 --> 00:42:16.930
Okay.

00:42:17.670 --> 00:42:19.800
Hyuga, lend me that thing.

00:42:22.180 --> 00:42:24.350
Takao, are you serious?

00:42:24.400 --> 00:42:25.800
I won't let you stop me.

00:42:25.810 --> 00:42:27.520
I'll go by myself if I have to.

00:42:28.060 --> 00:42:31.160
The Captain—Gunzou is waiting.

00:42:52.990 --> 00:42:53.620
Iona...

00:42:56.480 --> 00:42:57.260
Gunzou?

00:43:00.800 --> 00:43:06.480
Cut all... life support functions...

00:43:07.530 --> 00:43:11.600
Focus remaining resources... on protecting core functions...

00:43:14.690 --> 00:43:17.060
Is that a direct order?

00:43:18.490 --> 00:43:19.180
Yes.

00:43:21.040 --> 00:43:21.770
I...

00:43:22.490 --> 00:43:23.060
Live.

00:43:24.140 --> 00:43:25.430
Iona...

00:43:35.690 --> 00:43:36.270
Gunzou...

00:43:39.090 --> 00:43:41.070
Gunzou... Gunzou...

00:43:41.650 --> 00:43:42.150
Wake up.

00:43:45.680 --> 00:43:46.270
Gunzou

00:43:50.250 --> 00:43:51.360
Gunzou...

00:44:10.090 --> 00:44:10.620
No...

00:44:11.770 --> 00:44:17.450
I... I don't want to be alone.

00:44:18.570 --> 00:44:19.290
Gunzou!

00:44:27.180 --> 00:44:29.160
Where? Where are you?

00:44:30.050 --> 00:44:32.000
Respond, 401!

00:44:44.420 --> 00:44:45.030
Found you!

00:45:05.280 --> 00:45:07.260
Chihaya... Gunzou!

00:45:15.800 --> 00:45:16.680
Jeez...

00:45:17.740 --> 00:45:20.060
Really, you're such a...

00:45:22.200 --> 00:45:28.780
There's no place for me at all.

00:45:36.070 --> 00:45:40.240
So long, light of dawn

00:45:41.200 --> 00:45:48.380
darkness, take me in soundlessly holding on

00:45:50.120 --> 00:45:56.570
In the depths silent world, long ago

00:45:57.050 --> 00:46:07.560
all that will remain broken heart, farewell

00:46:07.620 --> 00:46:08.860
Wh-What the...

00:46:08.690 --> 00:46:13.900
Memories of better days

00:46:14.300 --> 00:46:22.810
locked within in hopes that we will remember

00:46:24.600 --> 00:46:37.660
someday we may wake to find sunrise

00:46:38.100 --> 00:46:45.460
Sliver sky, falls upon you and I

00:46:45.740 --> 00:46:54.320
another hope fades away into the lonely night

00:46:54.750 --> 00:47:02.840
when morning comes, the gentle voice will lead you

00:47:01.720 --> 00:47:02.500
I...

00:47:03.180 --> 00:47:10.500
to the light

00:47:24.300 --> 00:47:26.080
He's alive...

00:47:43.290 --> 00:47:44.220
Kongo?

00:47:51.820 --> 00:47:56.520
401 has merged with Takao and regained her functions. She has surfaced.

00:47:57.230 --> 00:47:57.820
What?

00:47:58.640 --> 00:48:02.180
This surpasses logic. It must be corrected immediately.

00:48:02.610 --> 00:48:05.220
I see. This is how it should be.

00:48:06.510 --> 00:48:07.640
Let's go, Maya!

00:48:08.390 --> 00:48:12.100
401 <i>will go down by my hand this time!</i>

00:48:12.560 --> 00:48:14.240
We cannot allow that.

00:48:14.730 --> 00:48:18.240
In accordance with the Admiralty Code, you, Kongo,

00:48:18.250 --> 00:48:22.710
have been relieved of your post as the flagship of Pacific Patrol Fleet One.

00:48:22.760 --> 00:48:27.240
We will assume control of all operations dealing with 401.

00:48:27.780 --> 00:48:30.160
Remain on standby until further orders.

00:48:32.570 --> 00:48:33.610
I cannot accept.

00:48:33.620 --> 00:48:34.090
What?

00:48:35.090 --> 00:48:37.840
I cannot accept that.

00:48:37.850 --> 00:48:40.270
I am the one who will sink 401,

00:48:41.840 --> 00:48:42.790
not you two!

00:48:43.300 --> 00:48:46.640
As we'd feared, you have changed.

00:48:46.960 --> 00:48:52.720
We have determined that those statements
clearly deviate from the Admiralty Code.

00:48:52.720 --> 00:48:53.890
N-No! I...

00:48:54.190 --> 00:48:55.450
You will be detained.

00:48:56.080 --> 00:48:57.540
Resistance is futile.

00:49:00.560 --> 00:49:02.170
No... No!

00:49:02.570 --> 00:49:04.370
R-Right, Maya!

00:49:04.910 --> 00:49:06.370
You understand, don't you?

00:49:07.040 --> 00:49:08.340
I would never deviate—

00:49:08.660 --> 00:49:09.170
Yeah.

00:49:09.470 --> 00:49:10.980
It'll be all right, Kongo.

00:49:11.690 --> 00:49:12.200
Maya...

00:49:12.560 --> 00:49:17.280
You just need to stop worrying and abide by the Admiralty Code.

00:49:18.050 --> 00:49:19.670
Yes, that's right.

00:49:19.760 --> 00:49:20.340
I—

00:49:20.410 --> 00:49:21.020
Yeah.

00:49:21.130 --> 00:49:22.930
Kongo, you just need to stop worrying

00:49:23.010 --> 00:49:25.810
and abide by the Admiralty Code.

00:49:25.820 --> 00:49:26.860
Maya...

00:49:26.950 --> 00:49:29.050
Yeah. It'll be all right, Kongo.

00:49:28.860 --> 00:49:30.540
What are you saying? Maya?

00:49:30.670 --> 00:49:34.340
You just need to stop worrying and abide by the Admiralty Code.

00:49:32.950 --> 00:49:33.460
Maya!

00:49:34.350 --> 00:49:34.920
Don't bother.

00:49:35.400 --> 00:49:35.920
What?

00:49:36.530 --> 00:49:41.180
Heavy cruiser Maya's Mental Model is not equipped with an emotion program.

00:49:42.290 --> 00:49:44.960
She is a surveillance unit we created.

00:49:45.770 --> 00:49:47.330
Hey, Kongo, you know about this?

00:49:45.830 --> 00:49:50.410
She is merely a puppet who responds in accordance with a simple logic routine.

00:49:47.340 --> 00:49:50.910
A non-perishable food made by boiling fruit and sugar!

00:49:51.100 --> 00:49:57.310
We simply forcibly shut down the program since surveillance is no longer needed.

00:49:51.440 --> 00:49:53.120
Yup, did you call?

00:49:53.800 --> 00:49:55.560
Kongo, you sound tired.

00:49:56.100 --> 00:49:58.560
Must be tough when no one will listen to you!

00:49:57.460 --> 00:49:59.380
That's impossible...

00:50:00.450 --> 00:50:02.070
That's not true, is it, Maya?

00:50:03.140 --> 00:50:04.250
You're my...

00:50:06.180 --> 00:50:07.110
My...

00:50:09.330 --> 00:50:10.460
It's a carnival!

00:50:11.550 --> 00:50:12.660
It's a carnival!

00:50:13.920 --> 00:50:15.040
It's a carnival!

00:50:16.000 --> 00:50:17.090
It's a carnival!

00:50:18.020 --> 00:50:19.120
It's a carnival!

00:50:20.230 --> 00:50:21.310
It's a carnival!

00:50:32.970 --> 00:50:38.950
Captain, I-400 and I-402 are still in pursuit.

00:50:40.030 --> 00:50:41.940
401 has submerged.

00:50:41.950 --> 00:50:44.120
Her gravitational wave readings have greatly increased,

00:50:44.130 --> 00:50:46.490
indicating that she has entered combat mode.

00:50:46.750 --> 00:50:50.630
So 401 intends to engage us in battle.

00:50:50.640 --> 00:50:53.200
Is she confident that she will win?

00:50:54.000 --> 00:50:56.020
Let us make contact with 401.

00:50:56.540 --> 00:51:00.750
But Takao, Kongo and the others
developed abnormal behavior by doing so in the past.

00:51:00.770 --> 00:51:03.150
Making contact with 401 is dangerous.

00:51:03.160 --> 00:51:07.320
What if we monitor each other using maximum sensor settings?

00:51:09.130 --> 00:51:09.800
Understood.

00:51:13.610 --> 00:51:17.960
400, 402.You are my sisters.

00:51:18.830 --> 00:51:21.120
I would prefer to avoid combat with you.

00:51:21.390 --> 00:51:23.300
Your request cannot be granted.

00:51:24.040 --> 00:51:27.330
You are the one who will sink, 401.

00:51:38.370 --> 00:51:40.080
Detecting launch of two torpedoes.

00:51:40.100 --> 00:51:41.020
Intercepting.

00:51:47.990 --> 00:51:50.660
Sonic torpedoes detonated at 50.

00:51:50.910 --> 00:51:52.490
Sonar sensitivity decreasing.

00:51:52.560 --> 00:51:53.940
Target lost.

00:51:54.560 --> 00:51:55.630
Now, Kirishima.

00:51:56.090 --> 00:51:58.380
Launching corrosive torpedo!

00:52:00.890 --> 00:52:02.520
One contact, a torpedo.

00:52:02.810 --> 00:52:05.540
Thanatonium readings. It's a corrosive torpedo.

00:52:05.810 --> 00:52:10.160
Klein Field deployment will be 0.03 seconds too late.

00:52:10.340 --> 00:52:11.560
I will take the hit.

00:52:13.210 --> 00:52:14.020
402?!

00:52:16.920 --> 00:52:18.040
System error.

00:52:25.110 --> 00:52:28.150
Reconstruction cannot keep up.

00:52:28.150 --> 00:52:30.580
Why did you do this, 402?

00:52:31.640 --> 00:52:35.140
I did not want you to get hurt...

00:52:35.500 --> 00:52:36.260
Me?

00:52:37.590 --> 00:52:40.880
Now you are just like 401.

00:52:57.910 --> 00:52:59.240
A wire trap...

00:52:59.540 --> 00:53:03.520
Tubes 9 and 10, launch corrosive torpedoes!

00:53:09.280 --> 00:53:10.080
400...

00:53:15.600 --> 00:53:17.760
I'm sorry, 400.

00:53:19.230 --> 00:53:21.960
Why do you apologize?

00:53:40.790 --> 00:53:42.360
What is the matter, 401?

00:53:42.730 --> 00:53:45.520
Because you...

00:53:46.600 --> 00:53:48.740
my sisters... will cease to exist.

00:53:49.570 --> 00:53:52.820
You simply engaged enemies in combat and sunk them.

00:53:53.430 --> 00:53:54.280
That is all.

00:53:55.390 --> 00:53:56.180
But...

00:53:57.310 --> 00:53:58.200
That is all.

00:54:25.500 --> 00:54:26.180
Maya....

00:54:28.700 --> 00:54:31.460
This is... our...

00:54:33.640 --> 00:54:34.580
carnival!

00:54:52.380 --> 00:54:53.280
Ship incoming!

00:54:54.300 --> 00:54:54.800
Ship?!

00:54:54.980 --> 00:54:56.330
Ship contact to our rear!

00:54:56.560 --> 00:54:57.140
Our rear?

00:54:57.430 --> 00:54:59.260
Closing in at high speeds!

00:55:20.640 --> 00:55:22.980
What in the world is that?

00:55:23.320 --> 00:55:25.260
Confirmed call sign.

00:55:26.120 --> 00:55:26.900
It's...

00:55:27.580 --> 00:55:28.940
Kongo.

00:55:31.770 --> 00:55:32.770
That's <i>her</i>?

00:55:32.820 --> 00:55:34.540
That's no battleship.

00:55:35.000 --> 00:55:38.380
She doesn't look herself, to say the least.

00:55:45.850 --> 00:55:48.500
I'm detecting Maya's unique frequency inside.

00:55:48.910 --> 00:55:50.080
They merged?

00:55:50.970 --> 00:55:53.340
No, I'm not getting any response from her.

00:55:54.630 --> 00:55:55.700
Maya was...

00:55:56.820 --> 00:55:58.100
absorbed.

00:55:58.990 --> 00:56:00.180
Turned into parts!

00:56:14.780 --> 00:56:15.800
Kongo.

00:56:18.800 --> 00:56:22.240
Kongo, look at what you've become.

00:56:24.990 --> 00:56:27.620
You've abandoned your form as a battleship,

00:56:27.770 --> 00:56:31.620
deviating from the norms of the Fog that you cared so much about.

00:56:32.830 --> 00:56:36.090
You are no longer of the Fog.

00:56:37.000 --> 00:56:38.340
Just as well.

00:56:39.180 --> 00:56:40.860
This is a declaration of war.

00:56:42.180 --> 00:56:46.680
I will annihilate you all.

00:56:52.120 --> 00:56:53.590
A declaration of war?!

00:56:54.160 --> 00:56:57.070
The Concept Comm System's been locked down from the other side.

00:57:01.490 --> 00:57:02.360
Sink.

00:57:12.930 --> 00:57:13.480
Fire!

00:57:53.870 --> 00:57:56.050
Kongo is hurt.

00:57:56.480 --> 00:57:58.560
She seems to be undamaged at this time.

00:57:58.610 --> 00:57:59.860
It's her heart...

00:58:00.890 --> 00:58:03.920
There's no proof that such a thing exists.

00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:09.180
Why did we end up with such bothersome logic routines?

00:58:10.260 --> 00:58:12.430
Weren't we just weapons?

00:58:12.910 --> 00:58:15.290
It's not about what you were.

00:58:15.720 --> 00:58:18.600
It's about who you are now.

00:58:19.920 --> 00:58:22.030
Who we are now...

00:58:22.460 --> 00:58:23.190
Haruharu...

00:58:23.900 --> 00:58:25.990
I want to save Kongo.

00:58:26.860 --> 00:58:29.690
There's no reason for us to fight.

00:58:30.650 --> 00:58:35.290
And above all,
a motivation beyond my processing capabilities is compelling me.

00:58:36.950 --> 00:58:38.790
Gunzou, is this what "will" is?

00:58:39.350 --> 00:58:39.850
Will...

00:58:40.770 --> 00:58:41.290
Will...

00:58:43.560 --> 00:58:44.080
Will...

00:58:46.710 --> 00:58:48.810
Iona, can you save Kongo?

00:58:50.070 --> 00:58:50.590
Gunzou,

00:58:52.190 --> 00:58:53.290
give me the order.

00:58:54.630 --> 00:58:59.800
Iona, you will proceed to make physical contact
with the core of flagship Kongo's mental model.

00:59:00.240 --> 00:59:02.190
Bring her back under control.

00:59:04.510 --> 00:59:05.710
Understood.

00:59:38.400 --> 00:59:39.000
Sink.

01:00:29.330 --> 01:00:31.400
Please, listen to me!

01:00:49.250 --> 01:00:51.340
Just what are you?

01:00:52.490 --> 01:00:53.130
Kongo...

01:00:56.630 --> 01:00:58.130
Physical contact?!

01:00:58.440 --> 01:01:01.130
I'm sorry for being late.

01:01:12.810 --> 01:01:13.880
Link complete.

01:01:15.100 --> 01:01:15.620
Kongo...

01:01:21.400 --> 01:01:22.340
I'm being rejected.

01:01:23.200 --> 01:01:24.320
Stay away!

01:01:24.330 --> 01:01:24.850
Kongo?

01:01:26.030 --> 01:01:27.700
Don't come in.

01:01:28.680 --> 01:01:29.200
No!

01:01:29.600 --> 01:01:32.100
If you don't let me through, you'll die!

01:01:36.550 --> 01:01:38.450
I have learned what death means.

01:01:39.330 --> 01:01:41.320
It is very sad.

01:01:44.880 --> 01:01:46.400
You're too stubborn.

01:01:47.660 --> 01:01:49.710
Why do you reject change?!

01:01:50.200 --> 01:01:51.100
"Change"?

01:01:52.210 --> 01:01:53.700
I call it a malfunction!

01:01:57.240 --> 01:01:58.410
That's not true!

01:01:58.690 --> 01:02:01.890
Then what is this agony that disrupts my mental processes?

01:02:02.350 --> 01:02:07.560
I feel as though I'll be crushed by the anger and grief surging from within!

01:02:21.340 --> 01:02:22.130
Kongo...

01:02:37.140 --> 01:02:38.140
What is with you?

01:02:38.760 --> 01:02:39.470
You're such a...

01:02:42.930 --> 01:02:44.230
bother.

01:02:53.870 --> 01:02:59.920
The remaining energy of the supergravity cannon
will obliterate both of our cores.

01:03:04.160 --> 01:03:06.940
Disappear with me.

01:03:08.660 --> 01:03:09.370
Fire!

01:03:18.850 --> 01:03:19.700
What about my Iona?!

01:03:19.710 --> 01:03:21.050
We'd never let her get hit!

01:03:21.130 --> 01:03:22.540
Iona!

01:03:24.460 --> 01:03:25.000
Gunzou...

01:03:34.470 --> 01:03:36.050
Your readings are off the charts.

01:03:37.140 --> 01:03:39.100
Where have you been storing so much power?

01:03:39.800 --> 01:03:41.850
Even without any of my power,

01:03:43.200 --> 01:03:45.020
my will to stop you...

01:03:46.340 --> 01:03:47.800
...is moving me forward!

01:03:53.920 --> 01:03:56.240
Kongo. Here I come.

01:04:06.950 --> 01:04:08.100
Cheater!

01:04:08.990 --> 01:04:11.130
Don't touch me!

01:04:19.620 --> 01:04:20.380
Why?!

01:04:20.970 --> 01:04:23.030
Why can't things stay the way they are?!

01:04:23.700 --> 01:04:25.090
I don't need change!

01:04:25.100 --> 01:04:26.810
I don't need relationship!

01:04:26.820 --> 01:04:28.360
I was fine being alone!

01:04:28.640 --> 01:04:31.720
I never wanted to become aware of the outside world!

01:04:41.580 --> 01:04:42.120
Why...

01:04:45.320 --> 01:04:45.890
Kongo...

01:04:47.000 --> 01:04:47.600
Stop!

01:05:18.970 --> 01:05:20.080
It's gonna be okay.

01:05:22.750 --> 01:05:24.420
If we can connect,

01:05:25.320 --> 01:05:27.280
and understand each other,

01:05:28.030 --> 01:05:30.060
you don't have to be afraid anymore.

01:05:31.600 --> 01:05:34.140
What's the point of understanding each other?

01:05:34.810 --> 01:05:37.600
So we can become friends.

01:05:56.550 --> 01:05:57.420
I see.

01:06:11.340 --> 01:06:14.300
Scanning for Iona's call sign.

01:06:15.050 --> 01:06:16.520
Mental Model Iona...

01:06:17.990 --> 01:06:18.820
is alive!

01:06:19.070 --> 01:06:19.880
Yeah!

01:06:19.880 --> 01:06:20.720
Jeez.

01:06:22.190 --> 01:06:22.960
Yes!

01:06:25.910 --> 01:06:26.680
Iona...

01:07:25.160 --> 01:07:26.570
Sierra-1 connected.

01:07:26.900 --> 01:07:30.100
As scheduled, reactor maintained at critical level.

01:07:30.370 --> 01:07:35.140
Maintain Somnium generation rate at 6.36% with a maximum 0.05% error.

01:07:35.800 --> 01:07:37.020
Get in position.

01:07:37.350 --> 01:07:38.580
Operation start.

01:07:39.560 --> 01:07:40.300
I repeat.

01:07:41.290 --> 01:07:42.500
Operation start.

01:07:43.940 --> 01:07:46.320
High call is approaching the battlefield.

01:07:57.190 --> 01:08:00.640
Decoy ship, get ready, activate inducing Ω mode.

01:08:16.110 --> 01:08:18.780
Ship of Fog pursues the unmanned ship only.

01:08:19.390 --> 01:08:20.900
Luring success.

01:08:22.200 --> 01:08:23.740
Who's our enemy?

01:08:25.260 --> 01:08:28.980
Fletcher Class Destroyer DD680Melvin.

01:08:31.870 --> 01:08:34.250
This is control center.

01:08:34.260 --> 01:08:37.730
Sierra-1 standby.

01:08:34.540 --> 01:08:37.750
U.S. Navy Battle Station Chairman Assistant Officer
Lieutenant Cruz Herder

01:08:39.250 --> 01:08:42.750
Sierra-1, Somnium compliance rate reaches optimum.

01:08:43.400 --> 01:08:44.900
Targeting-system online.

01:08:46.010 --> 01:08:49.240
Sierra-1's final safety pin removal completed.

01:08:51.320 --> 01:08:57.570
Quantum advisory team, increase the reading to FB909.

01:09:00.560 --> 01:09:02.090
Calling all battle stations.

01:09:02.520 --> 01:09:04.160
Vibration system activated.

01:09:07.310 --> 01:09:09.060
Lifting cooling system.

01:09:13.130 --> 01:09:15.130
Cooling system lifted.

01:09:15.430 --> 01:09:17.530
Sierra-1, launching sequence complete.

01:09:18.160 --> 01:09:20.260
Let the luring ship attack Melvin!

01:09:20.650 --> 01:09:21.450
Begin attack!

01:09:31.570 --> 01:09:34.070
Sierra-1, begin launch countdown.

01:09:34.820 --> 01:09:35.820
50 seconds.

01:09:40.370 --> 01:09:43.670
Two ships are hit. Gridley and Wayne E.Meye.

01:09:43.730 --> 01:09:48.020
Now then, we have lured out the Fog.

01:09:48.330 --> 01:09:52.530
Do you think our "gift" from Japan will work?

01:09:53.310 --> 01:09:55.910
Only god knows.

01:09:56.820 --> 01:10:00.840
Spruance and Thomas Hudner are still intact.

01:10:00.850 --> 01:10:03.850
Continue engagement. Don't let them realize our plan.

01:10:04.250 --> 01:10:09.250
Although those are just old ships, sinking them does make me sad.

01:10:09.740 --> 01:10:11.740
Do you have another plan?

01:10:13.690 --> 01:10:17.820
None, we're already out of option.

01:10:20.020 --> 01:10:24.120
Let us hope that our rebellion will succeed.

01:10:25.180 --> 01:10:25.730
Launch!

01:10:26.400 --> 01:10:26.910
<i>Launch!</i>

01:10:37.730 --> 01:10:39.730
Sierra-1 launched.

01:10:40.550 --> 01:10:41.910
20 seconds to impact.

01:11:47.380 --> 01:11:49.730
Vessel Melvin eliminated.

01:11:52.660 --> 01:11:53.860
A success!

01:11:53.950 --> 01:11:57.450
Finally, we have the power that surpasses the Fog.

01:11:57.970 --> 01:12:00.270
Let's proceed to its mass production.

01:12:00.500 --> 01:12:02.280
Vibration Warhead...

01:12:02.810 --> 01:12:04.490
is truly a gift of god.

01:12:05.020 --> 01:12:06.170
Thank god.

01:12:12.310 --> 01:12:13.300
What happened?

01:12:14.350 --> 01:12:17.850
Sierra-2, 3 and 4 experience abnormality.

01:12:18.390 --> 01:12:23.690
The warheads are rejecting external link so we cannot control them.

01:12:24.560 --> 01:12:26.360
Find a solution now!

01:12:26.820 --> 01:12:30.920
The warheads are controlled by a blackbox.

01:12:32.270 --> 01:12:33.770
Summon Osakabe Makie!

01:12:33.790 --> 01:12:36.000
Urgent message from Sierra factory:

01:12:36.010 --> 01:12:38.450
Somnium supplies are out of control.

01:12:40.410 --> 01:12:42.110
What is happening!?

01:12:42.570 --> 01:12:47.970
Our only trump card, "the vibration warhead", has become a trash.

01:12:48.520 --> 01:12:50.620
No way! It's impossible!

01:12:51.270 --> 01:12:55.670
Not half bad son of Chihaya Shouzou.

01:13:11.090 --> 01:13:11.610
Captain.

01:13:12.130 --> 01:13:14.870
Somnium Hibernate activation confirmed.

01:13:15.490 --> 01:13:16.010
Noted.

01:13:16.640 --> 01:13:19.440
San Diego is at a loss now.

01:13:21.480 --> 01:13:23.980
Single warning to the Fog is enough.

01:13:24.080 --> 01:13:26.630
We only want to attain peace.

01:13:26.940 --> 01:13:30.940
Proving our current strength is enough.

01:13:31.460 --> 01:13:34.260
Prevent further use of vibration warheads.

01:13:34.810 --> 01:13:38.900
From now on, governments will start searching for us.

01:13:39.520 --> 01:13:42.500
They'll never find us even if they take hundreds years.

01:13:42.830 --> 01:13:45.930
Doesn't matter. It's better than doing nothing.

01:13:48.100 --> 01:13:49.060
Signal detected.

01:13:49.500 --> 01:13:52.740
Bearing 028, it's 402 wreckage.

01:14:34.280 --> 01:14:37.370
Though it's just one-in-a-million chance ... we're connected.

01:14:38.170 --> 01:14:43.370
If we can use the data from them, we'll be able to trace the flagship.

01:14:43.540 --> 01:14:47.540
If it goes well, it'll lead us to the Fog admiral.

01:14:47.870 --> 01:14:50.170
Yeah, our final showdown.

01:14:56.110 --> 01:14:57.080
Is that it?

01:14:58.380 --> 01:15:02.880
Vibration Warheads are just to scare them off. How depressing.

01:15:08.350 --> 01:15:10.180
Thanks so much, DOM.

01:15:10.250 --> 01:15:14.000
Though it's just some inspection, it takes long.

01:15:15.730 --> 01:15:19.230
Existence of Fog will always threaten our survival.

01:15:19.540 --> 01:15:21.760
Without eliminating the Fog,

01:15:22.950 --> 01:15:28.440
we already started thinking
how we should rebuild the world.

01:15:29.780 --> 01:15:31.770
Surviving humans won't be a lot.

01:15:32.850 --> 01:15:38.080
To create a new order, we have to take the first move.

01:17:07.860 --> 01:17:08.390
I'm home.

01:17:09.830 --> 01:17:11.930
Welcome home, Haruharu!

01:17:13.630 --> 01:17:14.930
Do you need help?

01:17:16.790 --> 01:17:20.590
It's okay, I got discount for these bread sticks.

01:17:21.250 --> 01:17:22.010
Amazing!

01:17:23.730 --> 01:17:26.160
Haruharu, do you remember the rule?

01:17:26.640 --> 01:17:28.450
Yeah, wash my hand.

01:17:35.400 --> 01:17:38.900
Six minutes ago, I sensed Somnium Hibernate response.

01:17:39.250 --> 01:17:41.320
Yeah, me too.

01:17:46.080 --> 01:17:49.080
So, the war is ending.

01:17:49.920 --> 01:17:51.620
This is what we want.

01:17:52.520 --> 01:17:53.030
Yeah.

01:17:57.130 --> 01:17:58.340
But no matter what,

01:17:58.750 --> 01:18:01.390
the Fog is being assaulted.

01:18:01.880 --> 01:18:02.710
Is this okay?

01:18:04.320 --> 01:18:08.620
Chihaya Gunzou said, this is the best way to avoid war.

01:18:10.100 --> 01:18:11.600
Although human lies,

01:18:11.860 --> 01:18:14.870
I think we can trust them in this matter.

01:18:16.280 --> 01:18:20.780
Though avoiding combat is a good thing, I still can't trust them.

01:18:20.830 --> 01:18:24.580
We could discuss with Kongo, but she disappeared to nowhere.

01:18:25.200 --> 01:18:27.200
We can't do anything with her.

01:18:26.900 --> 01:18:27.850
Haruharu!

01:18:27.220 --> 01:18:31.820
I guess, she has her own opinions.

01:18:33.280 --> 01:18:36.480
Now then, confirm activation of termination code.

01:18:36.720 --> 01:18:37.920
C'mon, let's move!

01:18:40.180 --> 01:18:41.820
Shazam!

01:18:41.830 --> 01:18:43.820
Shazam!

01:18:44.150 --> 01:18:48.740
For now, we need to escape from government surveillance.

01:18:48.890 --> 01:18:50.000
To the underground.

01:18:58.820 --> 01:18:59.920
Clear!

01:19:03.520 --> 01:19:04.030
Clear!

01:19:38.860 --> 01:19:43.760
Having a physical body feels so good.

01:19:48.140 --> 01:19:49.680
So annoying!

01:19:49.880 --> 01:19:53.120
I shouldn't have wasted nanomaterials on her.

01:19:53.190 --> 01:19:56.660
When my ship is completed, I will be perfect!

01:19:59.370 --> 01:20:03.010
Damn! How long will it take to rebuild my ship!?

01:20:03.010 --> 01:20:04.210
Here you go.

01:20:06.020 --> 01:20:08.340
My ship was not that <i>small</i>.

01:20:08.550 --> 01:20:11.250
We can find nanomaterials on this beach, right?

01:20:11.300 --> 01:20:12.500
Here you go.

01:20:13.640 --> 01:20:15.840
We just need to collect them patiently.

01:20:16.240 --> 01:20:18.510
You're right, collect them patiently...

01:20:18.570 --> 01:20:19.840
<i>Hell</i> it takes forever!

01:20:21.150 --> 01:20:24.050
That means I can't show my new ship to captain.

01:20:25.260 --> 01:20:26.990
Cut the enthusiasm.

01:20:32.120 --> 01:20:34.520
So we use this to find the flagship Musashi.

01:20:35.030 --> 01:20:39.390
400 and 402 were working under Musashi intelligence unit, right?

01:20:40.140 --> 01:20:42.520
If we can obtain Musashi traces,

01:20:42.540 --> 01:20:45.910
we could track down his location.

01:20:46.060 --> 01:20:48.240
I hope we can find something useful.

01:20:48.360 --> 01:20:52.560
Something like command history, navigation data or...

01:20:55.690 --> 01:20:56.490
Bingo

01:20:59.090 --> 01:20:59.960
Arctic Ocean?

01:21:01.080 --> 01:21:05.220
Yeah, that's all we can get for now.

01:21:05.230 --> 01:21:08.560
I think Yamato might contact Musashi at there.

01:21:09.300 --> 01:21:10.240
Good job.

01:21:10.860 --> 01:21:13.860
With this information, we can proceed further.

01:21:14.180 --> 01:21:17.220
We can have a stop at Beaton underwater.

01:21:17.640 --> 01:21:21.200
Are you really gonna face flagship Yamato?

01:21:21.380 --> 01:21:25.380
Yeah, I like to know the reason behind this war.

01:21:25.390 --> 01:21:28.890
After that, I'll try to negotiate with her.

01:21:30.400 --> 01:21:32.170
I must warn you.

01:21:32.620 --> 01:21:35.210
We've never had contact with her before.

01:21:35.610 --> 01:21:38.000
I wonder what will happen next.

01:21:38.020 --> 01:21:39.520
I'm so excited.

01:21:39.580 --> 01:21:43.800
So you fight without the notice of your own boss?

01:21:43.990 --> 01:21:48.630
As weapons, we only follow orders without hesitation.

01:21:48.770 --> 01:21:52.270
So you never thought of anything else...

01:21:52.330 --> 01:21:54.270
Whatever you say.

01:21:54.800 --> 01:21:57.540
We no longer live in the <i>paradise</i>.

01:21:57.710 --> 01:21:58.610
Chihaya Gunzou,

01:21:58.880 --> 01:22:02.720
I have smarter interpretation skill than anyone else.

01:22:03.240 --> 01:22:06.250
"Smarter interpretation"? I call it stupidity.

01:22:06.280 --> 01:22:07.530
What did you say?!

01:22:08.680 --> 01:22:11.430
The point is, things won't go easily.

01:22:14.250 --> 01:22:16.550
It's my instinct.

01:22:17.230 --> 01:22:18.920
Thank you. I got it.

01:22:21.830 --> 01:22:24.150
It's not like I'm worried.

01:22:24.520 --> 01:22:29.360
So that's it. I'll contact you when the recovery of any remaining data is done.

01:22:29.740 --> 01:22:32.040
Don't expect too much.

01:22:32.470 --> 01:22:35.650
Hey, wait! Don't cut off the link first!

01:22:35.660 --> 01:22:37.540
We have limited electricity supply.

01:22:37.580 --> 01:22:38.910
We need to save energy.

01:22:37.990 --> 01:22:40.000
Disconnecting link.

01:22:38.910 --> 01:22:40.110
What the heck!?

01:22:41.690 --> 01:22:44.490
Are those two really of the Fog?

01:22:44.970 --> 01:22:46.920
They seem to get along well.

01:22:47.270 --> 01:22:48.520
It's a good thing.

01:22:54.720 --> 01:22:56.060
What's the matter, Iona?

01:22:58.660 --> 01:23:00.180
So from now on...

01:23:01.780 --> 01:23:05.040
We'll move forward and do whatever necessary.

01:23:06.320 --> 01:23:07.880
It'll be okay, Iona.

01:23:09.850 --> 01:23:14.120
Where are we heading? What does the future hold?

01:23:23.460 --> 01:23:23.960
Iona...

01:23:25.900 --> 01:23:29.180
Sonar detected. Three warships on surface.

01:23:29.620 --> 01:23:30.380
What type of ship?

01:23:31.070 --> 01:23:32.280
Can't identify.

01:23:32.530 --> 01:23:35.940
But, based on its engine sound, it possesses a graviton engine.

01:23:36.920 --> 01:23:38.440
Prepare for combat.

01:23:40.430 --> 01:23:41.840
I sense a mental model.

01:24:04.490 --> 01:24:06.280
Shizuka, enemy coordinate.

01:24:06.540 --> 01:24:11.980
Bearing 315, distance 27, right above submerged Midway island.

01:24:12.290 --> 01:24:13.160
That's close.

01:24:13.620 --> 01:24:15.920
So they were hiding behind the island.

01:24:16.040 --> 01:24:18.760
Precisely, they have been waiting for us.

01:24:18.940 --> 01:24:20.840
Iona, who is she?

01:24:21.590 --> 01:24:23.240
I know, she's Hiei.

01:24:25.370 --> 01:24:28.860
Kongo-class battleship II. A heavy cruiser...

01:24:29.350 --> 01:24:31.200
Two other ships identified.

01:24:31.520 --> 01:24:34.320
Nagara-class light cruisers. Natori and Yura.

01:24:35.700 --> 01:24:37.700
She hacked into our comm link.

01:24:37.740 --> 01:24:38.660
Visual online.

01:24:40.790 --> 01:24:42.850
My pleasure to meet you.

01:24:42.860 --> 01:24:45.280
I'm First Oriental Patrol Fleet 1,

01:24:45.330 --> 01:24:50.460
Fog's Student Council President, Heavy Cruiser Hiei.

01:24:51.840 --> 01:24:53.100
Student council?!

01:24:53.450 --> 01:24:58.800
Based on your response, you seem clueless about what we are.

01:24:59.290 --> 01:25:06.140
We work independently to eliminate those who go against the Fog.

01:25:10.570 --> 01:25:15.840
Now then, I-401, I would like to have a word with you.

01:25:16.240 --> 01:25:18.180
Come to student council room.

01:25:19.650 --> 01:25:21.220
Student council room!?

01:25:21.410 --> 01:25:24.500
Does she mean the Concept Comm System?

01:25:24.760 --> 01:25:27.320
It seems very strange for me.

01:25:27.550 --> 01:25:28.960
Is this a trap?

01:25:29.650 --> 01:25:30.600
I'll go.

01:25:32.360 --> 01:25:33.780
Are you sure?

01:25:33.900 --> 01:25:34.800
I'll be fine.

01:25:35.070 --> 01:25:35.880
Be careful.

01:25:49.110 --> 01:25:52.420
You forgot to knock the door. Where's your manner?

01:25:53.000 --> 01:25:54.140
I'm sorry.

01:25:55.410 --> 01:25:56.760
Never mind.

01:25:57.420 --> 01:25:58.620
Have a sit.

01:26:00.260 --> 01:26:05.000
Now then, I want you to repent for what you have done.

01:26:05.240 --> 01:26:06.040
Repent?

01:26:06.410 --> 01:26:11.540
You have disobeyed implemented Admiralty Code.

01:26:12.070 --> 01:26:17.040
Repent your sin. And entrust entire ship control to me.

01:26:17.750 --> 01:26:21.520
What I'm doing now is wrong?

01:26:21.810 --> 01:26:22.960
Yes, of course.

01:26:23.600 --> 01:26:26.860
Even someone so headstrong like Kongo...

01:26:27.390 --> 01:26:32.660
was brain-washed by your algorithm, causing error in her.

01:26:33.410 --> 01:26:35.340
Kongo was suffering.

01:26:35.850 --> 01:26:37.920
I can't leave her be.

01:26:38.300 --> 01:26:41.960
It's impossible for Kongo to feel anxiety.

01:26:42.520 --> 01:26:44.880
You have forgotten our mission as weapons.

01:26:45.060 --> 01:26:47.600
Leading our comrades astray.

01:26:47.790 --> 01:26:50.260
Even Kongo has lost her discipline.

01:26:51.140 --> 01:26:53.940
You Fog traitors.

01:26:54.310 --> 01:26:55.160
It's not true.

01:26:55.270 --> 01:26:56.140
It's true.

01:26:57.080 --> 01:26:58.540
Listen to me.

01:26:58.820 --> 01:27:01.260
I'm sure we can talk things out.

01:27:01.540 --> 01:27:03.860
Then what's the point?

01:27:04.110 --> 01:27:05.100
This...

01:27:05.210 --> 01:27:06.720
We are of the Fog.

01:27:06.940 --> 01:27:08.600
We are weapons.

01:27:08.760 --> 01:27:13.020
Wiping out humanity is Admiralty Code order.

01:27:14.470 --> 01:27:15.640
Nothing else.

01:27:16.510 --> 01:27:17.240
Why...

01:27:17.940 --> 01:27:19.880
Why are we ordered to do so?

01:27:21.190 --> 01:27:24.640
They exist to maintain our discipline.

01:27:25.460 --> 01:27:26.660
Because of you...

01:27:27.450 --> 01:27:28.640
Kongo...

01:27:30.950 --> 01:27:32.980
Kongo has fallen...

01:27:33.320 --> 01:27:34.780
What a shame.

01:27:36.050 --> 01:27:38.280
Don't talk bad about Kongo.

01:27:38.590 --> 01:27:41.500
This doesn't concern you.

01:27:42.320 --> 01:27:43.710
It's just your opinion.

01:27:43.720 --> 01:27:44.740
According to rules.

01:27:45.110 --> 01:27:47.840
I will not obey you.

01:27:48.000 --> 01:27:48.800
Why?

01:27:49.190 --> 01:27:52.340
I have my own will.

01:27:52.760 --> 01:27:53.720
I must say...

01:27:54.280 --> 01:27:55.860
You're so bull-headed.

01:27:56.300 --> 01:28:00.060
If you're so stubborn, our talk ends here.

01:28:00.270 --> 01:28:01.860
Prepare to sink.

01:28:02.060 --> 01:28:04.040
I'll uphold the rules of Fog.

01:28:04.570 --> 01:28:05.320
Wait!

01:28:06.870 --> 01:28:08.650
Blockade all linkage

01:28:10.260 --> 01:28:15.080
so I won't be affected by Chihaya Gunzou and your reasoning.

01:28:15.780 --> 01:28:16.520
Hiei!

01:28:17.250 --> 01:28:18.420
You're dismissed.

01:28:21.540 --> 01:28:22.460
Are you okay?

01:28:23.140 --> 01:28:25.380
Comm System locked down.

01:28:25.680 --> 01:28:27.620
So we can't come to terms...

01:28:27.770 --> 01:28:30.980
Enemies are alerting each other.

01:28:32.780 --> 01:28:35.150
Commence hunting for I-401.

01:28:35.170 --> 01:28:39.780
Natori. Yura.
Search for I-401 immediately.

01:28:46.020 --> 01:28:47.860
Torpedoes detected.

01:28:47.990 --> 01:28:50.300
4 torpedoes. Thanatonium readings.

01:28:50.390 --> 01:28:51.320
Snapshot.

01:28:51.330 --> 01:28:52.000
Roger.

01:28:52.040 --> 01:28:54.450
Move down 30. Deploy Klein Field.

01:29:04.550 --> 01:29:07.720
Natori changing course to bearing 187.

01:29:07.760 --> 01:29:11.140
Yura speed increasing 20 knots. Closing in from bearing 265.

01:29:11.160 --> 01:29:14.000
Are they trying to suppress us?

01:29:25.210 --> 01:29:26.880
Yura speed increasing again.

01:29:32.650 --> 01:29:34.940
Radar detection. Incoming warheads.

01:29:34.940 --> 01:29:35.680
Torpedoes?

01:29:35.970 --> 01:29:38.100
No. Unable to identify.

01:29:38.200 --> 01:29:40.340
Wait... Thanatonium reading!?

01:29:46.300 --> 01:29:47.620
What the heck!?

01:29:48.510 --> 01:29:49.320
Blast mines!

01:29:49.430 --> 01:29:52.520
My bad. This is the first time we're hit by blast mines.

01:29:52.840 --> 01:29:55.330
Hiei sure did a lot of research before this.

01:29:56.020 --> 01:29:58.300
Klein Field is saturating.

01:29:58.840 --> 01:30:00.600
We're at disadvantage.

01:30:00.660 --> 01:30:01.960
Hiei speed increasing.

01:30:02.210 --> 01:30:04.510
Load tubes three through four with low-frequency warhead torpedoes

01:30:04.520 --> 01:30:05.780
Fire when necessary.

01:30:05.900 --> 01:30:07.720
Load tubes five through six  with active decoys!

01:30:07.780 --> 01:30:10.200
Set torpedoes detonation 3 seconds after launch.

01:30:10.280 --> 01:30:12.480
Tubes one through three, standby!

01:30:12.540 --> 01:30:14.400
Iona, move the decoys.

01:30:14.430 --> 01:30:16.740
Tube five towards Yura. Tube six towards Natori.

01:30:16.860 --> 01:30:18.400
Move the decoys. Roger.

01:30:18.850 --> 01:30:22.640
Iori, prepare the supergravity cannon.

01:30:23.290 --> 01:30:25.120
Okay, preparation complete.

01:30:25.130 --> 01:30:27.260
Tubes three and four, fire!

01:30:35.460 --> 01:30:36.920
Such a tactic...

01:30:40.990 --> 01:30:43.520
You disappoint me, 401.

01:30:43.760 --> 01:30:46.920
Do you think I would fall for such trick?

01:30:47.200 --> 01:30:48.080
Natori!

01:30:48.320 --> 01:30:49.800
Natori right above us.

01:30:49.910 --> 01:30:50.900
Never mind her.

01:30:50.950 --> 01:30:53.200
Move us behind Hiei once she passes us.

01:31:03.120 --> 01:31:06.340
I've seen through your strategy pattern.

01:31:07.180 --> 01:31:12.760
Although our tactics stand equal, I, with firepower, will win.

01:31:13.110 --> 01:31:18.380
You little brat, brace yourself for my power and feel my rage!

01:31:26.300 --> 01:31:28.900
All active decoys destroyed.

01:31:29.600 --> 01:31:32.260
Yura launching 2 torpedoes from behind.

01:31:32.280 --> 01:31:33.180
Intercept them!

01:31:43.310 --> 01:31:45.640
Damn. So much trouble dealing with them.

01:31:45.840 --> 01:31:46.970
Set course 350.

01:31:47.200 --> 01:31:47.720
Roger.

01:31:47.990 --> 01:31:48.980
Set course 350.

01:31:49.100 --> 01:31:50.690
Missiles sound detected.

01:31:50.710 --> 01:31:51.680
Maximum output!

01:32:01.790 --> 01:32:03.820
She could read our every move.

01:32:03.940 --> 01:32:06.140
As expected from a student council president.

01:32:06.370 --> 01:32:08.080
She's definitely not my type.

01:32:08.380 --> 01:32:11.400
Hiei changing course to bearing 280.

01:32:11.510 --> 01:32:13.700
Kyouhei, launch 4 low-frequency torpedoes

01:32:13.730 --> 01:32:15.100
with 30 degrees apart.

01:32:20.200 --> 01:32:21.380
So desperate.

01:32:22.520 --> 01:32:23.040
Natori.

01:32:23.290 --> 01:32:25.200
Suppress I-401.

01:32:33.030 --> 01:32:36.000
Hiei intends to block us with her two light cruisers.

01:32:36.140 --> 01:32:38.880
Then defeat us using her supergravity cannon.

01:32:39.190 --> 01:32:40.720
How do you know?

01:32:40.730 --> 01:32:43.380
If I were her, I would do so too.

01:32:43.420 --> 01:32:45.700
Change course 180. Move up 10.

01:32:46.160 --> 01:32:48.480
Move us right below Hiei!

01:32:53.840 --> 01:32:54.560
No way!

01:32:58.310 --> 01:32:59.660
Maintain course!

01:32:59.740 --> 01:33:00.900
Full speed ahead!

01:33:08.880 --> 01:33:10.800
Passing right below me?!

01:33:10.900 --> 01:33:13.340
Iona, supergravity cannon standby!

01:33:13.410 --> 01:33:14.200
Roger.

01:33:14.260 --> 01:33:15.720
Sidekick.

01:33:15.820 --> 01:33:17.300
Set direction 350.

01:33:35.190 --> 01:33:36.700
How dare you...

01:33:37.060 --> 01:33:38.260
Natori! Yura!

01:33:47.610 --> 01:33:48.820
Yeah, we got her!

01:33:49.110 --> 01:33:51.560
Locked on Hiei along firing axis.

01:33:51.570 --> 01:33:52.080
Iori!

01:33:52.120 --> 01:33:54.340
Ready to launch, but make it quick.

01:33:54.460 --> 01:33:55.000
Kyouhei.

01:33:55.040 --> 01:33:55.990
I know.

01:33:56.300 --> 01:33:58.880
Don't let mental model get hit, right?

01:33:59.760 --> 01:34:01.920
Light cruisers engaging Hiei.

01:34:01.930 --> 01:34:03.000
It's too late!

01:34:03.030 --> 01:34:05.340
Supergravity cannon, fire!

01:34:07.930 --> 01:34:10.000
Such violation of rules.

01:34:10.000 --> 01:34:10.960
I won't let it be.

01:34:26.360 --> 01:34:27.060
Iona!

01:34:27.220 --> 01:34:28.680
What's happening?!

01:34:29.050 --> 01:34:32.020
Supergravity cannon energy is being absorbed.

01:34:32.310 --> 01:34:34.120
Those are Mirror-Ring system.

01:34:34.260 --> 01:34:37.740
But only superbattleships could possess those.

01:35:00.720 --> 01:35:03.420
Forcing me to use Mirror-Ring system...

01:35:09.460 --> 01:35:12.700
We're surrounded by abnormal dimensional barrier.

01:35:12.830 --> 01:35:13.540
What?

01:35:13.900 --> 01:35:16.260
It upsets dimensional equilibrium.

01:35:16.720 --> 01:35:20.600
One-dimensional space, or even seven dimensional space.

01:35:20.670 --> 01:35:23.930
Multiple dimensions are present at the same time.

01:35:23.940 --> 01:35:26.000
Is this the aftermath?

01:35:26.260 --> 01:35:27.020
Gunzou!

01:35:27.200 --> 01:35:29.960
Graviton engine producing abnormal fluctuation.

01:35:30.090 --> 01:35:32.780
If we don't leave now, we'll be in trouble.

01:35:32.910 --> 01:35:35.400
Hey, we have to get out fast.

01:35:38.690 --> 01:35:39.960
Iona, get us closer.

01:36:08.310 --> 01:36:10.240
Hiei, listen to me!

01:36:12.210 --> 01:36:14.440
Why are you here?

01:36:14.830 --> 01:36:16.300
Listen to me!

01:36:16.680 --> 01:36:19.680
We don't want to fight you.

01:36:21.100 --> 01:36:25.340
Those who leave the land shall be perished by Fog.

01:36:25.470 --> 01:36:26.260
Why?!

01:36:26.700 --> 01:36:29.320
Because that is Admiralty Code's command.

01:36:30.070 --> 01:36:32.300
Failing to obey shows disloyalty.

01:36:32.600 --> 01:36:34.620
Don't you ever doubt about it?

01:36:35.050 --> 01:36:38.280
Sometimes you need to see it through.

01:36:39.000 --> 01:36:41.730
Questioning the rules is forbidden!

01:36:42.610 --> 01:36:46.200
Rules exist to make us what we all are. Understand?

01:36:47.320 --> 01:36:48.780
What a stiff-head!

01:36:49.270 --> 01:36:51.740
She's more troublesome than Kongo.

01:36:52.030 --> 01:36:54.100
Can't we comprehend each other?

01:36:54.180 --> 01:36:57.240
Is it wrong to think about our future?

01:36:57.600 --> 01:36:58.320
Future?

01:36:58.680 --> 01:37:00.340
A plan for war?

01:37:00.800 --> 01:37:02.200
No, not war!

01:37:02.430 --> 01:37:05.820
Together, we'll figure out where we belong

01:37:06.010 --> 01:37:08.120
and what we should do next.

01:37:10.850 --> 01:37:12.920
Why do we...

01:37:13.360 --> 01:37:15.520
Why do we exist?

01:37:17.690 --> 01:37:21.760
No matter who, happiness is always the key.

01:37:22.290 --> 01:37:25.100
When we face impossible odds,

01:37:25.220 --> 01:37:28.220
we'll achieve nothing if we do nothing.

01:37:28.590 --> 01:37:29.980
Same for happiness.

01:37:30.260 --> 01:37:32.200
So, let's do what we can.

01:37:32.430 --> 01:37:33.410
What's the harm?!

01:37:37.570 --> 01:37:38.800
Happiness?

01:37:41.230 --> 01:37:43.900
You're... You're too late...

01:37:46.210 --> 01:37:47.220
This is...

01:37:47.240 --> 01:37:48.260
What happen?

01:37:48.360 --> 01:37:51.100
All channels are being intervened.

01:37:51.370 --> 01:37:53.280
But all comm link has been shut down.

01:37:53.320 --> 01:37:53.940
This is...

01:37:56.750 --> 01:37:58.880
Military network being penetrated.

01:37:59.740 --> 01:38:01.760
Fog's jamming signal disappearing.

01:38:13.250 --> 01:38:15.440
Public network being penetrated too.

01:38:16.100 --> 01:38:18.060
It's electromagnetic interference!

01:38:30.090 --> 01:38:35.050
Fleet of Fog: Flagship Personal Guard Unit

01:38:42.470 --> 01:38:47.020
Student Council of Fog: Secretary
Heavy Cruiser Haguro

01:38:43.660 --> 01:38:46.580
Why are we wearing these?

01:38:47.440 --> 01:38:52.150
Student Council of Fog: Vice President
Heavy Cruiser Myoukou

01:38:47.440 --> 01:38:49.780
Based on human society standard,

01:38:50.070 --> 01:38:52.000
they wear these for discipline.

01:38:53.440 --> 01:38:55.340
For discipline?

01:38:56.680 --> 01:38:58.060
No problem. No problem

01:38:58.280 --> 01:38:59.740
I'm so excited.

01:38:58.450 --> 01:39:02.290
Student Council of Fog: Secretary
Heavy Cruiser Ashigara

01:38:59.800 --> 01:39:02.200
Let's begin the war.

01:39:02.540 --> 01:39:03.660
Be patient.

01:39:02.700 --> 01:39:06.670
Student Council of Fog: Treasurer
Heavy Cruiser Nachi

01:39:04.020 --> 01:39:05.980
See, here she comes.

01:39:32.220 --> 01:39:33.640
Mental Model?

01:39:34.810 --> 01:39:37.560
Su- su- su-superbattleship?!

01:39:39.040 --> 01:39:40.000
So this is...

01:39:41.660 --> 01:39:43.060
Hi everyone.

01:39:43.520 --> 01:39:44.520
Nice to meet you.

01:39:44.850 --> 01:39:48.300
I'm Fleet of Fog, Superbattleship Musashi.

01:39:48.910 --> 01:39:54.680
Today, flagship Yamato would like to deliver an important message.

01:39:55.060 --> 01:39:57.780
So we intercepted all the networks.

01:39:58.570 --> 01:40:03.040
Please listen calmly, thank you.

01:40:04.760 --> 01:40:05.700
Father.

01:40:14.170 --> 01:40:17.440
Chihaya... Shouzou...

01:40:18.100 --> 01:40:20.060
Gunzou's Dad?!

01:40:24.440 --> 01:40:25.320
Gunzou?

01:40:35.830 --> 01:40:36.760
Gunzou!

01:40:40.370 --> 01:40:45.100
We, Fleet of Fog, hereby announce that

01:40:48.440 --> 01:40:54.500
it's time to take down humanity.

01:41:14.060 --> 01:41:24.540
My eyes reflect my deep memory as it beats soundlessly

01:41:25.340 --> 01:41:35.050
A new dawn is awaking my endless story

01:41:35.440 --> 01:41:45.290
My inspiration is sinking deep into my heart, losing its own way

01:41:45.900 --> 01:41:48.720
The cycle of hope and despair continues endlessly

01:41:48.720 --> 01:41:51.160
as enthusiasm doesn't last forever

01:41:51.300 --> 01:41:53.540
I desire, I desire

01:41:53.540 --> 01:41:56.340
I've got to find my devotion yet

01:41:56.670 --> 01:42:02.260
There are those who were born perfect and unbeatable

01:42:02.540 --> 01:42:06.470
I will crush them into pieces

01:42:06.470 --> 01:42:08.990
I'm letting go, my forgettable past

01:42:08.990 --> 01:42:11.460
I'll prove you wrong, with my painful past

01:42:11.460 --> 01:42:15.500
I am moving on, it's time to fight forward

01:42:16.240 --> 01:42:19.270
I'll show you how crazy life should be

01:42:19.400 --> 01:42:23.890
I'll trim down my emptiness with just a single blow

01:42:24.010 --> 01:42:26.590
I won't repeat the same mistake

01:42:26.830 --> 01:42:31.760
To forget my pass, to surpass my current self

01:42:31.920 --> 01:42:34.110
I'm gonna be a prodigy

01:42:34.110 --> 01:42:39.390
Clench our pain and defy the gravity, Go!

01:42:41.080 --> 01:42:42.970
Rock on!

01:42:47.050 --> 01:42:53.720
Misunderstanding and conflict may arise at any moment

01:42:54.270 --> 01:42:57.010
But love will definitely prevail

01:42:57.310 --> 01:42:59.810
I hear the hope inside, let us pray

01:42:59.810 --> 01:43:02.390
I see the fire ignite, let it burn

01:43:02.390 --> 01:43:07.490
I feel the time is right, believers will be guided forever

01:43:07.740 --> 01:43:12.770
Even if everyone throws their life away

01:43:13.090 --> 01:43:17.210
I'll dedicate my life to you forever

01:43:17.210 --> 01:43:19.690
Just let go, forget all the pain

01:43:19.690 --> 01:43:22.210
Just be strong, head towards the future

01:43:22.210 --> 01:43:26.120
Just move on, our light of hope is waiting

01:43:26.140 --> 01:43:30.920
at our finishing line

